00:00:59.910 --> 00:01:01.470
and I watched that John Oliver clip

00:01:01.470 --> 00:01:04.383
and started to go down a rabbit hole.

00:01:05.330 --> 00:01:07.913
(upbeat music)

00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:12.780
Subway shows up a lot in Korean dramas.

00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:14.220
Not just like one or two,

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:18.480
but like five, 10, 15,
almost 20 different shows

00:01:18.480 --> 00:01:21.960
have product placement
from Subway sandwiches.

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:23.310
The American fast food chain

00:01:23.310 --> 00:01:25.680
that is apparently the largest

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:29.130
fast food chain in the
world by store locations.

00:01:29.130 --> 00:01:29.963
What?

00:01:29.963 --> 00:01:30.796
What is going on here?

00:01:30.796 --> 00:01:33.690
Subway is not cool, it is not good,

00:01:33.690 --> 00:01:36.693
and yet K-dramas are full of Subway.

00:01:41.910 --> 00:01:43.380
We gotta get to the bottom of this.

00:01:43.380 --> 00:01:45.870
Is there something special
about Korean Subway?

00:01:45.870 --> 00:01:47.010
Like is it different?

00:01:47.010 --> 00:01:47.880
Am I missing something?

00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:49.830
Is there something better
about Korean Subway

00:01:49.830 --> 00:01:51.000
versus American Subway?

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:53.430
Because if there is I
want to know about it.

00:01:53.430 --> 00:01:54.993
So first, let's settle that.

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:01.980
I'll do mozzarella, hot chili,

00:02:01.980 --> 00:02:03.033
salt and pepper.

00:02:12.655 --> 00:02:15.540
Okay, after that very scientific study

00:02:15.540 --> 00:02:18.270
which by the way was a
little bit scientific

00:02:18.270 --> 00:02:20.430
because I did choose the specialty items

00:02:20.430 --> 00:02:22.590
that only exist in Korea
and not in America,

00:02:22.590 --> 00:02:24.300
and I chose something that had beef in it

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:26.640
which is a thing that
Korea does really well.

00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:28.020
So I tried to give South Korea

00:02:28.020 --> 00:02:29.970
the best chance of being differentiated,

00:02:29.970 --> 00:02:34.920
and the result is that it
is kind of better, kind of.

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:36.570
- Eat fresh.

00:02:36.570 --> 00:02:37.950
Eat fresh.

00:02:37.950 --> 00:02:38.970
- Eat fresh.

00:02:38.970 --> 00:02:39.840
- That's my man.

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:40.740
- But not really.

00:02:40.740 --> 00:02:43.110
It's like still just microwaves

00:02:43.110 --> 00:02:46.110
and like mass produced
industrial ingredients

00:02:46.110 --> 00:02:47.340
prepared in front of you.

00:02:47.340 --> 00:02:48.930
They kind of taste old and stale,

00:02:48.930 --> 00:02:50.880
kind of delicious at the same time.

00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:51.720
I don't know.

00:02:51.720 --> 00:02:53.490
But the thing I noticed at this location

00:02:53.490 --> 00:02:55.050
and several others that I've visited

00:02:55.050 --> 00:02:56.820
in my short time here in Seoul

00:02:56.820 --> 00:03:00.450
is that these subways
look and feel different.

00:03:00.450 --> 00:03:02.910
Cleaner, more sleek, well lit.

00:03:02.910 --> 00:03:04.860
So yeah, I guess you could say

00:03:04.860 --> 00:03:07.170
that Subway sandwiches taste better

00:03:07.170 --> 00:03:08.520
when you're eating them here

00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:10.080
instead of here.

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:11.910
Okay, this is not what
this video is about.

00:03:11.910 --> 00:03:13.200
It's not about whether or not

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:15.300
Korean Subway is better
than American Subway,

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:16.200
you can decide that.

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:18.750
I'm interested in how Subway sandwiches

00:03:18.750 --> 00:03:21.210
has taken over Korean dramas.

00:03:21.210 --> 00:03:22.650
There is an explanation for this.

00:03:22.650 --> 00:03:24.480
I talked to an expert in this topic

00:03:24.480 --> 00:03:26.340
who's like the guy to explain it.

00:03:26.340 --> 00:03:28.380
He's a communications and media professor

00:03:28.380 --> 00:03:30.330
at one of the best universities in Korea,

00:03:30.330 --> 00:03:31.500
and he has thoughts on this.

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:34.050
But first, I have to do the thing

00:03:34.050 --> 00:03:35.880
that allows me to make these videos

00:03:35.880 --> 00:03:39.360
which is tell you about the
sponsor of today's video.

